WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.880
A working synapse needs a release apparatus lined up with the right receptors.

2
00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.320
Adhesion proteins span the gap, and some organize both sides.

3
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.020
They can do more than hold cells together.

4
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.520
Each contact has to specify what kind of synapse it will be.

5
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.120
Glutamate and GABA synapses sit on the same dendrite, each with its own receptors.

6
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.580
Scaffolds gather those receptors.

7
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.820
Astrocytes add signals that help synapses form and respond.

8
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.900
Neurexin sits on the axon.

9
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.320
Neuroligin is its partner on the receiving side.

10
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.320
Put neuroligin on a kidney cell in a dish.

11
00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.940
Axons touching it gather vesicles and release and retrieve them.

12
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.520
Control cells do not induce this.

13
00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:54.540
Neurexin on a non-neuronal cell can also cluster postsynaptic proteins in touching

14
00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.540
dendrites. Organization runs both ways.

15
00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:04.403
On the receiving side, PSD-95 holds neuroligin and NMDA receptors.

16
00:01:05.443 --> 00:01:08.083
AMPA receptors reach this scaffold through stargazin.

17
00:01:08.903 --> 00:01:10.803
Stargazin brings them to the cell surface.

18
00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:15.283
Its tail binds PSD-95 and holds them at synapses.

19
00:01:16.283 --> 00:01:22.543
In stargazer cerebellar granule cells, synapses keep NMDA responses but lack AMPA

20
00:01:22.543 --> 00:01:28.763
responses. Inhibitory synapses use gephyrin to anchor glycine receptors and many

21
00:01:28.763 --> 00:01:29.943
GABA-A receptors.

22
00:01:31.117 --> 00:01:34.257
Astrocyte signals separate building from responding.

23
00:01:35.257 --> 00:01:40.497
Purified retinal ganglion cells barely communicated until glial signals were added.

24
00:01:41.617 --> 00:01:45.137
Conditioned medium increased transmission without increasing survival.

25
00:01:46.157 --> 00:01:50.937
Thrombospondins induce synapses that look normal and release transmitter, yet have

26
00:01:50.937 --> 00:01:52.797
no AMPA receptor responses.

27
00:01:53.777 --> 00:01:59.317
Other astrocyte factors, including glypicans 4 and 6, recruit AMPA receptors and

28
00:01:59.317 --> 00:02:00.757
make such synapses respond.

29
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:05.530
Now distinguish what a protein can do from what the animal needs.

30
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.430
Neuroligin is sufficient to induce terminals in a dish.

31
00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:15.430
Yet mice lacking neuroligins 1, 2 and 3 had normal synapse numbers in the brainstem,

32
00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.050
with impaired transmission.

33
00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.290
The assay tests induction.

34
00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.870
The deletion separates synapse number from function.

35
00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:26.190
Normal counts do not mean normal communication.

36
00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:29.483
Finally, a synapse keeps changing.

37
00:02:30.363 --> 00:02:35.223
In immature rodent hippocampal and cortical neurons, high internal chloride makes

38
00:02:35.223 --> 00:02:42.483
GABA depolarize. As KCC2 rises, internal chloride falls and GABA hyperpolarizes.

39
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:45.763
Depolarizing does not always mean exciting.

40
00:02:45.763 --> 00:02:49.803
GABA-A channels can still inhibit by shunting current.
